The 100G receiver interfaces are discovered by mapping `mlx5_0` and `mlx5_1`
through `ibdev2netdev`. The per-host `spectral_line_100g_interfaces` inventory
variable is used only when automatic discovery returns no interfaces. The
SR-IOV sender address is queried live from the interface named by `Sender_Nic`.
The BMC IP is read locally with `ipmitool lan print`.
